<title>TURKEY: Turk Arcelik 96 profits jump 189 pct.</title>
<headline>Turk Arcelik 96 profits jump 189 pct.</headline>
<dateline>ISTANBUL 1997-03-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>1996 final results</p>
<p>(billion lira unless stated)</p>
<p>    Per share profit (lira)   1,289.72  vs    668.93</p>
<p>    Net profit		    8,705.60  vs  3,010.17</p>
<p>    Net sales		    87,448.80  vs 49,472.33</p>
<p>    Operating profit	   12,951.41  vs  7,269.24</p>
<p>    Exceptional income	  2,378.25  vs    757.50</p>
<p>    Exceptional expense	   876.91  vs  1,307.76</p>
<p>    Interest Paid		 3,350.55  vs  2,254.96</p>
<p>    Total debts		  27,558.57  vs 14,612.08</p>
<p>    Equity			 22,075.47  vs 10,789.60</p>
<p>    Capital			 6,750.00  vs  4,500.00</p>
<p>NOTE - Turkey's leading durables producer Arcelik A.S. is largely owned by the leading industrial conglomerate Koc Holding.</p>
<p>The company plans to distribute a 300 lira cash dividend per 1,000 lira nominal share from its 1996 profits from May 30 after approval at the annual meeting of shareholders and directors on April 3.</p>
<p>It also plans to raise capital to 10,125 billion lira by issuing 3,375 billion lira of bonuses, or 0.5 bonus per 1,000 lira nominal share. 1,350 billion lira of the bonuses will be financed by additional dividends from 1996 profits and the rest from other company funds.</p>
<p>The figures above do not take into account Turkey's 84.9 percent wholesale inflation in 1996.</p>
<p>-- Istanbul Newsroom +90-212-2750875</p>
</text>
